# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The collection itself never goes in this repository.
#
# This repository is public so that GitHub Pages can serve the site for free,
# which means anything committed here is readable by anyone. The encryption in
# docs/ protects the published site; it does nothing for files sitting in the
# repository. So the archive stays on Lucas's machine and only the encrypted
# output is committed.
#
# Keep your own backup of everything below. GitHub is not holding a copy.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The source of truth and everything derived from it
coin-archive/coin-archive/inventory.csv
coin-archive/coin-archive/catalog.html
coin-archive/coin-archive/photos/
coin-archive/coin-archive/sheets/

# The identifications and bag assignments — these carry the same data as the CSV
coin-archive/coin-archive/seed_pass*.py
coin-archive/coin-archive/assign_bags*.py
coin-archive/coin-archive/assign_bag16_finds.py
coin-archive/coin-archive/mark_duplicates.py

# Stray duplicates that used to sit at the repository root
/catalog.html
/inventory.csv

# Local build state: the salt, and a check value that catches a mistyped
# passphrase on a rebuild. Not a secret, but not worth publishing either.
vault.json

# Windows "downloaded from the internet" metadata
*:Zone.Identifier
*.Identifier

# macOS
.DS_Store

__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The collection README lives with the collection, not in the public repo
coin-archive/coin-archive/README.md
